artifact.self_contained_problem:
Consider the quadratic complex Hénon map $H_2 : \mathbb{C}^2 \to \mathbb{C}^2$ defined by
$$H_2(x, y) = (y,\, x + y^2).$$
The point $(0,0) \in \mathbb{C}^2$ is a fixed point of $H_2$. The differential $DH_2(0,0)$ has eigenvalues equal to the two roots of $\lambda^2 = \lambda \cdot 0 + 1$, namely the golden-ratio-type values $\lambda_{\pm} = \tfrac{1 \pm \sqrt{5}}{2}$; in particular one eigenvalue is hyperbolic expanding and the other is hyperbolic of absolute value less than $1$, but the fixed point is not linearizable in the usual sense over $\mathbb{C}$ because of resonances/parabolic-like obstructions arising from the algebraic relations among the eigenvalues, and the global polynomial nature of $H_2$ leads to subtle behavior of stable and unstable manifolds in a full neighborhood of the origin.

Problem: Give a complete description of the local dynamics of $H_2$ in a neighborhood of the origin in $\mathbb{C}^2$. In particular, describe:
\begin{itemize}
\item the structure of the local stable and unstable manifolds $W^s_{\mathrm{loc}}(0)$ and $W^u_{\mathrm{loc}}(0)$ and their intersection behavior;
\item whether there exist orbits of $H_2$ that remain in an arbitrarily small neighborhood of the origin for all positive and negative iterates (i.e., points in $\bigcap_{n\in\mathbb{Z}} H_2^n(U)$ for arbitrarily small open neighborhoods $U$ of the origin) other than $0$ itself, and if so what is their structure;
\item the existence or non-existence of small periodic cycles, homoclinic/heteroclinic tangencies, and invariant analytic/Fatou objects accumulating at the origin;
\item a normal form or conjugacy class describing $H_2$ restricted to a neighborhood of $0$ in $\mathbb{C}^2$.
\end{itemize}

